              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Aaron Rhodes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was delicious - the combination of plum jam and horseradish! I will definitely make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2016-09-28T23:49:19.137Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nightfall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is really, really good. It has become a regular weeknight dinner. I've used plum preserves, kumquat jam, Asian pear jam, and mango preserves in the recipe. All work well. I usually use boneless chicken breasts, simply because that's usually on hand.",
            "datePublished": "2016-02-12T13:09:47.080Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Donna Nissani"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was easy and fantastic! We had company for dinner and I am a little nervous about trying something new for guests, but this didn't disappoint. I added the garlic as was suggested and we had frozen horseradish that I grated with a fine cheese grater. We will do this again!",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-17T17:38:22.320Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JARRIE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This had a very nice flavor. I added a little garlic. I think it would be better if you rubbed a little oil on the skin before the baking, so the skin would crisp up a little, or do this on the grill, or use skinless meat -- as written the skin stays kind of squishy which we found unappealing personally. Any jam would probably work -- I used orange marmalade and served this with AR's \"Sweet and Spicy Green Beans\". Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-04T16:01:19.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
